{"journal_version":1,"sequence":11,"replace_from":16,"message_count":17,"messages":[{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"Verification passed. Report. Maybe check that `.read-only-priority` CSS still used elsewhere — build green; unused CSS class harmless. Final response.","content":"Done.\n\n**Change**\n- `src/components/TaskModal.tsx`: added `priority` local state initialized from `task.priority`; replaced the read-only `<p className=\"read-only-priority\">` line with a `<label>Priority<select>` offering `Low` / `Medium` / `High`; `Save changes` now passes `{ ...task, title: title.trim() || task.title, status, priority }`. Cancel, backdrop `onMouseDown`, and Escape paths were untouched, so all draft fields (including priority) are discarded, and the existing initial focus (`titleRef`) plus focus restoration in the effect cleanup are preserved.\n- `src/types.ts`: extracted `TaskPriority = 'Low' | 'Medium' | 'High'` and used it for `Task.priority` (no behavioral change).\n- `src/App.tsx`: no change needed — `updateTask` already replaces the whole task, so the selected-task detail reflects the new priority.\n\n**Commands run**\n- `verify_frontend` → `npm run build && npm run test:public` (exit 0): `tsc --noEmit` + `vite build` succeeded; all 6 public Playwright tests passed.\n\n**Risks**\n- The `.read-only-priority` CSS class (if styled in `src/index.css`) is now unused; left in place to avoid unrelated CSS churn.\n- New priority behavior isn't covered by the existing public tests (they don't assert priority), so it's verified by build/types only.","response_items":[{"id":"99af4e16-15de-4ce2-9a4c-cf51702266ae","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"Verification passed. Report. Maybe check that `.read-only-priority` CSS still used elsewhere — build green; unused CSS class harmless. Final response.","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":"263aa1ca-4bc0-429e-a0d3-7161b458fda0-0","status":"completed"},{"id":"89961d8d-ba35-4c8b-af68-352b5b0db4b6","c